# Python bytecode from the gen_*.py data-pipeline scripts. Was tracked, so
# every script run dirtied the tree; untracked and ignored 2026-07-28.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# [M27A] Imported map data — ALL regenerable build output.
#
# The whole directory is generated: 421 per-map JSON files plus the
# _preview/_above validation renders. `python3 scripts/gen_map_import.py all`
# reproduces it deterministically from the reference clone.
#
# Ignored as a DIRECTORY rather than by file pattern so a new kind of
# generated output can't quietly start being tracked.
#
# NOTE: the reference clone is itself gitignored above, so a fresh checkout
# needs the clone in place before this can be regenerated — see CLAUDE.md's
# "Ground truth / reference" section.
#
# What is NOT ignored: assets/map_atlases/. Those are shared per tileset pair
# (60 pairs for 421 maps), are runtime dependencies of tracked scenes, and
# follow Godot convention of committing texture + .import together.
assets/maps/
